<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie0559245c2908c0c578bf9c67cde8f56486920e7" commit="21463bdb85a1a82ed3c718227162cd42da5c9267" commit_message="[autotest] Fix use of RetryingConnection  The .Execute method returns the number of rows found, not the results of Fetchall().  BUG=chromium:764822 TEST=Tested locally  Change-Id: Ie0559245c2908c0c578bf9c67cde8f56486920e7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/665324 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="665324" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/24/665324/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9fe1f3ffaf9c36e426dfb2b311394158b458436a" commit="2f5b880e9597ceb0a38dad73893d5eeb6bc31e72" commit_message="[autotest] mysql_stats: Fix gauge/counters  Some metrics which were Counters should actually be gauages (row lock time avg and row lock time current waits are not events, they are gauages). Also, added a row_lock_waits counter, which is a counter of the total number of queries that had to wait on a row lock.  BUG=None TEST=Tested locally  Change-Id: I9fe1f3ffaf9c36e426dfb2b311394158b458436a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/666228 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="666228" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/28/666228/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Iaaed6816a033cfa2e71c206c65dd7b97b7e477c5" commit="6e5f0e89d01cea4137049906907a8ca99ec9915f" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: i915: temporarily disable DP MST support by default&quot;  This reverts commit d26b8f3fb5f6c4bb8465576c2647bd6d0b13c8ec.  This enables MST on i915 on kernel 4.4-based devices.  BUG=chromium:764601 TEST=boot eve  Change-Id: Iaaed6816a033cfa2e71c206c65dd7b97b7e477c5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/665966 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="665966" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/665966/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I47d39f179a0481ac7fc509b609797ae748587055" commit="4afe202b20155aab6509fde9bac71bdcf064b03f" commit_message="cbuildbot: Tweak --local and --remote messages.  We recently removed --local and --remote tryjob support from cbuildbot, but the messaging to help people who use the wrong tryjob command didn't work out right. Fix it!  BUG=chromium:762676 TEST=run_tests -q  Change-Id: I47d39f179a0481ac7fc509b609797ae748587055 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/666005 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="666005" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/05/666005/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4c501882a3594abb5e9f372ae898cbbb908213a1" commit="c6ebd116af8390b7f8dfd8cb190726663e17dd85" commit_message="cli: Add 'cros moblabvm'  `cros moblabvm`  is a new CLI command for managing moblab VMs. It allows the user to create a workspace where VM images are created from chromiumos test images. Then, this workspace can be used to launch two VMs -- a moblab VM and a VM for a DUT attached to the moblab.  BUG=chromium:725620 TEST=Use the new CLI; unittests.  Change-Id: I4c501882a3594abb5e9f372ae898cbbb908213a1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/646974 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="646974" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/74/646974/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia2f5a2ff034a6b7b96f7bd4f3b42bf5645a05aed" commit="5518fe49431d097ad77dcc9213d807f2a3ca6140" commit_message="i2c: rand of i2ctest console command is unsigned  We use rand to get timestamp counter low word and do random test (test_dev = rand % i2c_test_dev_used). But we will get a negative index (test_dev) if low word larger than 0x80000000 and cause the array to access the wrong locations and trigger an exception.  This change also fix following error: error: i2c_s_test may be used uninitialized in this function [-Werror=maybe-uninitialized]  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=&quot;forcetime 0 0x80000000&quot; then &quot;i2ctest&quot;, no exception triggered.  Signed-off-by: Dino Li &lt;Dino.Li@ite.com.tw&gt; Change-Id: Ia2f5a2ff034a6b7b96f7bd4f3b42bf5645a05aed Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/663110 Reviewed-by: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="663110" owner_email="Dino.Li@ite.com.tw" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/10/663110/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0f5478cb46f6b362f035545e6c67aea1366a7d86" commit="1adba28c00545ae88edf1bc794ab460a5306573f" commit_message="Add feature detection for certain kit features  Autotest can now query GetCapabilities to find out what kits can do.  Also, move GetChipName-&gt;GetAdvertisedName as it was confusing.  BUG=chromium:752719 TEST=Run this code on the Chameleon board, with both kits attached: $ make &amp;&amp; make remote-install CHAMELEON_HOST=$CHAMELEON_IP Execute the non-flaky non-stress tests that use this code, see that the tests pass: $ test_that --board ${BOARD} --args &quot;chameleon_host=${CHAMELEON_IP}&quot; \ ${DUT_IP} bluetooth_AdapterPairing.{,le.}mouse \ bluetooth_AdapterPairing.{,le.}mouse.pairing_twice \ bluetooth_AdapterHIDReports.{,le.}mouse  Change-Id: I0f5478cb46f6b362f035545e6c67aea1366a7d86 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/658697 Commit-Ready: Alexander Lent &lt;alent@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Lent &lt;alent@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="658697" owner_email="alent@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/chameleon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/chameleon" ref="refs/changes/97/658697/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id22bfd94dbe870ed3c92c9b9f78148710701bff7" commit="c7a9eabb9bd8168805919fec523f84dc1a256d20" commit_message="auto_updater: increase KERNEL_UPDATE_TIMEOUT to 180 seconds.  There has been changes in eve that causes the update engine to start much later in the boot process. In addition we increased the size of the rootfs (and kernel too?) and th